# pnpm + Next.js on Netlify (OpenNext adapter)
#
# Netlify runs a strict, Linux-native pnpm install. pnpm's default *isolated*
# layout (a .pnpm symlink store) does not expose transitive/vendored packages at
# the top level the way Next.js expects, which surfaces during `next build` as:
#     Unable to read file react-server-dom-turbopack-client.d.ts
# (a vendored type stub that lives deep inside the `next` package and resolves
# through node_modules). Netlify's own docs require hoisting for pnpm + Next.js:
#   https://opennext.js.org/netlify  ->  "pnpm support"
#
# `public-hoist-pattern[]=*` hoists every dependency to the top-level
# node_modules (equivalent to `pnpm install --shamefully-hoist`), giving Next the
# flat, npm-like resolution it expects. It is safe for local builds too.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*
